  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nToday and tonight, the flow aloft will transition from an upper \nridge to SW flow aloft across Montana. Meanwhile, an upper trough\nmove into the Canadian Rockies and Pacific NW. The pattern change \nwill lead to increasing daily chances for showers and thunderstorms,\nwith heavy rain potential as some southwestern monsoonal moisture\ndoes transport its way this far north. \n\nThere will be chances for showers and thunderstorms at times\ntoday. Chances for showers and thunderstorms increase tonight  \nwith widespread rain expected between Thursday, Thursday night and\nFriday morning with heavy rain possible at times. The current\nprobability for one inch or more rain between tonight and Friday\nis 60 to 80 percent across NE Montana. The probability for 2 or\nmore inches of rain between tonight and Friday is between 10 and\n40 percent. If more than 2 inches of rain occurs, flooding could\nbecome a possibility depending on how quickly the rain falls in a\ngiven location. WPC currently has a slight risk of excessive\nrainfall for NE Montana Thursday and Friday at this time. Will\nhold off on any Flood Watches for now given that the ground is dry\nand rainfall has been light over the last 4 weeks. \n\nFlow aloft Friday night and Saturday turns into a drier WSW aloft\nas the upper trough moves east across the Canadian Prairies.\nRain chances diminish Friday afternoon and Friday night and\nSaturday look mainly dry with isolated showers possible. \n\nFrequent waves moving across eastern Montana will bring shower and\nthunderstorm chances at times early next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nGenerally tweaked pops tonight and Thursday to provide better hour\nto hour consistency in rain chances. \n\nLow confidence in shower and thunderstorm chances today. Confidence\nin precipitation chances increase tonight and Thursday and are\nhigh Thursday night and Friday morning. High confidence in many\nareas getting an inch or more rain overall but low confidence\npossibility of amounts higher than an inch.",
